    "show_share": true,
    "description": "Different varieties of viral hemorrhagic fevers are found throughout the world. The one most prevalent to this region is the Congo Crimean virus. Symptoms include high fever and body aches, followed within a few days by bleeding from the nose, mouth, ears, lungs or rectum. The virus has been most prevalent in Balochistan. It call be contracted through infected animals and patients' blood and body fluid secretions. There is currently no proven cure for the disease, and most patients die of bleeding complications.",
